Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Four-, Five- and Six-Point QED: Construction and Checks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"5ca1b447-bdbb-4884-877e-3bc950bf458e"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate Setup once, then evaluate the individual calculations below. \
Canonical photon-helicity representatives are sufficient for the C++ export: \
it combines them into one process and supplies equivalent placements by \
relabeling identical particles. Each result has a distinct qed4..., qed5... \
or qed6... variable, so later calculations do not overwrite it. The wrapper \
displays progress, total time and all final checks before returning a \
validated expression. All momenta are ingoing. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.003241743408349*^9, 
  4.0032424221545486`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"456f9b3b-17be-418a-8209-\
5779a70c7365"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"4816341a-7984-4b8b-988a-1a38dedfcf65"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
hepcatDirectory = ExpandFileName[\"~/code/hepcat\"];
$HEPCATpath = FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"source\"}];
Get[FileNameJoin[{$HEPCATpath, \"HEPCAT.wl\"}]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002798488237926*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"502400f7-a148-4769-998b-3289c5a54045"],

