Cell["\<\
The independent tests use the constructive expressions above. Full export and \
validation diagnostics remain in eeeeAExport; a reference formula is never \
substituted. If an export already exists, add \"Overwrite\" -> True \
deliberately to refresh it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a3084c36-4c28-4b1c-8752-49ff83d9120b"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Six-Point Amplitudes (Max Spurious)", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0028158424031563`*^9, 
  4.0028158469914503`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4ef2e3e5-8308-4e9c-b3bb-\
4b0a4f3fa343"],

Cell["\<\
Twenty-one separate calculations: all sixteen four-photon helicity \
assignments, all four two-photon assignments with four fermions, and \
six-fermion scattering. Some mixed-helicity calls retain a two-hour \
factorization budget; this is a limit, not a finishing-time guarantee. \
Unresolved calculations must not be interpreted as validated amplitudes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2df3f600-d020-4c7e-bfb6-0d45658a8f43"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["e,E,A.+,A.+,A.+,A.+", "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002276980342226*^9, 
  4.002276980644375*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b07060a5-2eb9-47cc-b325-\
48dfc1171d25"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate the construction cell to combine adjacent same-helicity emissions in \
pairs. The resulting expression has complexity 120 and passes all 23 checks.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"de0a6c14-5fdf-4251-8b11-b470bf78af9a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
qed6PPPP = ConstructAmplitude[
  {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\"},
  diagramModel, factorizationModelSpurious,
  \"PolePreference\"->\"AllSpurious\",
  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel]\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002276983351096*^9, 4.002276983627392*^9}, {
  4.002277223897098*^9, 4.002277224658288*^9}, {4.002280936248722*^9, 
