There are no external photons in this process, so the result has only \
physical poles even under Max Spurious. The constructor groups the two \
attachment orders on each central fermion line over their common photon \
propagators. The compact result has complexity 3168 and passed all 21 checks. \
Evaluate the cell to regenerate the expression used by the MadGraph check and \
C++ export below.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"49a9367c-f914-4280-990c-da1657450d45"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
qed6SixFermions = ConstructAmplitude[
  {\"e\", \"E\", \"e\", \"E\", \"e\", \"E\"},
  diagramModel, factorizationModelSpurious,
  \"PolePreference\"->\"AllSpurious\",
  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel]\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
